[ti:Twinkle Twinkle Little Star]
[ar:Dcoetzee]
[al:Public Domain Voices]
[by:Navis demo library, CC0 1.0 timings; text: Jane Taylor, The Star (1806), public domain]
[length:02:05]
[00:00.39]Twinkle, twinkle, little star,
[00:04.98]How I wonder what you are!
[00:09.45]Up above the world so high,
[00:13.89]Like a diamond in the sky.
[00:18.61]Twinkle, twinkle, little star,
[00:23.06]How I wonder what you are!
[00:27.60]When the blazing sun is gone,
[00:32.10]When he nothing shines upon,
[00:36.75]Then you show your little light,
[00:40.96]Twinkle, twinkle, all the night.
[00:45.49]When the blazing sun is gone,
[00:50.19]When he nothing shines upon,
[00:54.86]Then the trav'ller in the dark,
[00:59.16]Thanks you for your tiny spark,
[01:03.92]He could not see which way to go,
[01:08.47]If you did not twinkle so.
[01:13.08]Then the trav'ller in the dark,
[01:17.71]Thanks you for your tiny spark,
[01:22.35]In the dark blue sky you keep,
[01:26.64]And often thro' my curtains peep,
[01:31.41]For you never shut your eye,
[01:36.09]Till the sun is in the sky.
[01:40.64]In the dark blue sky you keep,
[01:45.21]And often thro' my curtains peep,
[01:49.97]'Tis your bright and tiny spark,
[01:54.73]Lights the trav'ller in the dark:
[01:59.61]Tho' I know not what you are,
[02:02.52]Twinkle, twinkle, little star.
